    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0096" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg774"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 399.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 3d of September, No.
                    341, has been received.</p>
                <p>Reserving, for the present, remarks upon the political aspect of the reception of
                    the Florida at Brest, I have submitted the despatch to the Secretary of the
                    Navy, and asked his consideration of your suggestion, in regard to sending a
                    force to intercept the Florida on her leaving that harbor.</p>
                <p>I will make the Secretary’s decision known to you as soon as it shall have been
                    received from him.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm.</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
